A||||3||mshill||1.6:1 Rockers and Torque?||||5||
Z||000000||mshill||11-07-2000||06:03 PM||||I am starting to work on my 3.4 pushrod and was wondering if putting 1.6:1 ratio rockers into it would reduce the torque?<P>If I was to put 1.6:1 rockers on the intake ports only, what would that do?  <P>In my 86SE rebuild I put the GM Performance cam into it and it feels like it lost a little low end power, but pulls strong through 5000 RPM.  I want to maintain or increase the lowend power as opposed to the <BR>top speed.||||reg||5
Z||000001||88formula||11-07-2000||08:34 PM||||According the Dyno2000 you will gain about one horsepower @ 5000 rpm and 1 ft. lb. of torque @ 4500 rpm on a performance 3.4-liter engine (.427 intake lift to .455 lift).||||reg||1
Z||000002||88formula||11-07-2000||08:44 PM||||That GM performance 12363220 camshaft will work great with your 3.4-liter engine. It is what I am using in mine. Expect about 169 horsepower @ 5000 rpm and 212 ft. lbs. of torque @ 3000 rpm. On a stock 2.8 that camshaft would make 154 horsepower @ 5500 rpm and 176-ft. lbs. or torque @ 3500-4000 rpm. I got 134 horsepower @ 4500 rpm and 180-ft. lbs. of torque @ 3000 rpm with a completely stock 2.8-liter engine for a baseline.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Terrybogin||11-07-2000||10:43 PM||||I wonder if the old racer's trick of running higher ratios only on the corner cylinders holds true for 6 cylinders too? ||||reg||1
